  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Greater Port Vila Urban Resilience Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will improve urban resilience in Greater Port Vila (GPV) through capacity building, institutional strengthening, and the construction of two multipurpose emergency shelters. The project is guided by the Greater Port Vila Resilient Urban Development Strategy and Action Plan (GPV RUDSAP) which envisions, that by 2030, Greater Port Vila is safe, inclusive, resilient, and a vibrant economic hub based on sustainable development. About 53% of the total project financing is from disaster risk reduction sources. About 15,500 people in the municipality of Port Vila will benefit from the project, of which about half are women.

The project also supports efforts to recover from the impacts of the coronavirus disease (COVID-19) pandemic and Tropical Cyclone Harold through (i) preventive measures for health and social safety nets; (ii) a focus on the vulnerable, women and the &quot;new poor&quot;; and (iii) partnerships and investments that generate jobs and stimulate the local economy.</narrative>
  </description>
